# .secretlintignore — paths secretlint should NOT scan
#
# This file OVERRIDES the shared .mega-linter.d/.secretlintignore template. The
# runner stages a shared sub-config only when the repo has no file of the same
# name, so this is a wholesale replacement, not a merge. Every entry the
# template carries must be repeated here or it is silently lost.
#
# Format: gitignore-style glob patterns, one per line. `**/` anchors a pattern
# at any depth. Lines starting with `#` are comments.
#
# Curation principle (from the shared template): only ignore content that is
# (a) derived, (b) known to produce false positives at high volume, or (c)
# explicitly excluded from linting elsewhere in this config. Do NOT add broad
# source-tree exclusions — secretlint is most valuable when it sees as much of
# the real code as possible.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependency lockfiles
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Lockfiles contain integrity hashes and registry URLs that pattern-match
# secret-like tokens (long hex strings, base64-looking digests). They are
# generated, never source-of-truth for credentials.
**/package-lock.json
**/yarn.lock
**/pnpm-lock.yaml
**/Pipfile.lock
**/poetry.lock
**/Cargo.lock
**/go.sum
**/composer.lock

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Linter and test outputs (derived artefacts, not source)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A SARIF file can contain literal "secret-looking" snippets that triggered
# OTHER scanners — running secretlint over those creates a noisy feedback loop.
#
# megalinter-reports/ also has to be listed here because secretlint runs with
# cli_lint_mode: project, walking the workspace itself rather than taking
# MegaLinter's filtered file list. That bypasses IGNORE_GITIGNORED_FILES, so
# gitignoring the folder is not enough on its own. Scanning it is additionally
# a race against the run in progress: secretlint enumerated
# megalinter-reports/copy-paste/jscpd-report.html, jscpd rewrote it mid-scan,
# and the read failed with ENOENT.
**/megalinter-reports/**
**/.test-output/**
**/coverage/**

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test fixtures (canonical false-positive source)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test data routinely embeds fake tokens, sample JWTs, and example API keys to
# exercise parser and security paths. These are intentionally secret-shaped but
# never real credentials. Scope kept narrow — only fixture directories, not
# entire test trees, so real test code is still scanned.
**/testdata/**
**/test/fixtures/**
**/tests/fixtures/**
**/__fixtures__/**

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI assistant directories
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local-only developer configurations, already excluded from the broader linter
# scan via ADDITIONAL_EXCLUDED_DIRECTORIES. Mirrored here so secretlint stays
# consistent with the rest of the suite.
**/.agents/**
**/.cache/**
**/.claude/**
**/.cursor/**
**/.opencode/**
**/.specify/**
**/.uf/**

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Repository-specific exclusions
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python virtual environments.
.venv/
venv/

# Evaluation harness fixtures carry deliberately planted fake secrets that the
# review council is scored on finding; snapshots quote them verbatim as
# evidence. Fixing them breaks the test cases.
.lola-eval/

# lola package manager install tree: third-party modules, gitignored and
# regenerated by `lola mod update`. Not this repository's source. The hits here
# are a secret-scanner module's own detection-rule test fixtures.
.lola/
